{
  "id": "T18_55_an_explicit_end_act_naming_the_fixture_policy_is_checked_against_its_derivation",
  "family": "T18",
  "rules": [
    "7.7.5",
    "10.2.9",
    "7.6.5",
    "7.6.10",
    "8.1.2",
    "9.5.8"
  ],
  "description": "A change story governed by the fixture policy has a directive whose lacquer requirement is outstanding. An application's end act naming the fixture policy with cause directive_closed at the review, and one with cause review at the review, both differ from the reference's own derivation of the policy and are rejected; neither gives an ignore as its record. When the requirement is fulfilled, maintenance records the policy end act; writing it again with identical content is a replay. A revise of it naming the policy with a later time differs from the derivation and is rejected.",
  "note": "7.7.5: \"an implementation that implements the policy rejects an explicit end act naming it, or a `revise` of one, whose content differs from its own derivation of that policy (10.2.9).\" README section 7: \"An explicit end act naming the fixture policy, or a revision of one, is compared with the reference's own derivation of that policy, and one that differs fails `10.2.9` on that ground alone, whether or not its content also gives an ignore as a `record` (7.7.5, 10.2.9)\"; \"An identical write of a generated one is a replay\". The ignore case is T18_37.",
